; Test: What happens when ONE max sink gets MULTIPLE matches?
; This is the true non-determinism question for HE/MeTTa compatibility

(score alice 85)
(score bob 92)
(score charlie 78)

; Single exec with pattern that matches multiple times
(exec 0
  (, (score $name $value))
  (O (max (highest-score $m) $m $value)))

; Question: Does max see ALL matches before finalizing?
; Or does it process them one at a time?
;
; Expected behavior for max/min sinks:
; - sink() is called for EACH match
; - All values accumulate in self.max
; - finalize() outputs the single maximum
;
; So we should get: (highest-score 92)
